 "novel_mechanics_found": "Round 8 refuted every remaining candidate mechanism for the D/8 twin and discovered the fail-timer. (1) FAIL-TIMER: the row-63 bar is a level fail-timer. It accrues ~1 tick per ~10 actions passively, PLUS +1 per refused/stranding big-B press. At 64 ticks the NEXT stranding B-press is FORCED THROUGH instead of refused: the phase advances, the unsupported avatar is destroyed, and the game enters GameState.GAME_OVER. (2) RECOVERY: after GAME_OVER, a RESET action (action 0) resumes at the START of the current level with levels_completed retained (5) and a zeroed timer - death costs 1 action plus level-restart. The level restart restores ALL consumed sockets (R2 B/A socket, right-room 8-socket), re-hides the quad and 8-bar, unlatches the assembly, returns the ring home, and resets LM to 6/7. (3) QUAD IS LM-ONLY, +1 CYCLE: clicking any quad button while standing on the LAUNCHER checker still advances only the lower-middle checker (out-of-order click test confirmed +1-cycle semantics, not set-to-color); the other three checkers are fixed-type. No way to retype another checker into D/8. (4) TELEPORT NETWORK IS A STAR CENTERED ON LM: a fixed checker's 6-click fires ONLY when LM currently has that checker's type (launcher checker with LM=6/7: nothing; R1 checker with LM=9/A: nothing). There is no hidden second twin behind any fixed checker, including no R1->goal-room-B-block pairing. (5) D/8 6-click does NOT teleport to the big 8-ring: tested with ring at home, ring displaced 4 up, and post-latch - all null. The latch-merge event itself creates no D-colored cell anywhere (full-grid scans). (6) BARE RING OBEYS THE ASSEMBLY MOVEMENT LAW AND MORE: up-2 from home refused (rows<=25 must be void), and an east drive at rows 26-33 was refused at target cols 30-37 even though all covered cells were wall/void at rows>=26 - the real confinement is TIGHTER than round 7's stated law; the ring/assembly appears confined to the central void-shaft neighborhood (cols ~6-33) and can never reach the goal room band. (7) THE MOVING C PLATFORM (cols 16-21) is phase-coupled: rows 56-57 at most phases, rows 54-55 at phase P5 - it is what supports the avatar at (18,54) during P5. Standing on it and clicking big-6 with LM=6/7, D/8, C/B, and 9/A all teleport nothing: it is support material only. (8) NO HIDDEN SOCKETS remain: R2 lower half (rows 20-23, cols 4-9), corridor west (cols 6-9), and the full LM interior (rows 48-53, cols 18-29) were exhaustively walked with per-step full-grid diffs - zero reveals. (9) available_actions on every L6 frame is exactly [1,2,3,4,6]: ACTION5 is not even legal input. (10) The goal sprite IS the solid B block at (46,6) rows 6-7 cols 46-47 inside the goal room (adapter hand_verifier goal attr) - touching it is the win condition. The D/8 twin creation mechanism remains undiscovered after exhausting the entire visible control surface.",
 "narrative": "Replayed the banked 322-action L5 prefix from fresh reset; frame_level==5 confirmed. Then replayed round 7's actions 322-448 to resume at its R2/quad-revealed state (avatar in R2, assembly unlatched, ring home) instead of re-deriving - 448 steps total at the cut. From there, in order: (a) quad-button semantics test - each button advanced LM by +1 in the 6/7->D/8->C/B->9/A cycle; an out-of-order click (qA from 6/7 -> D/8) proved +1-cycle, not set-to-color; (b) swept R2 lower half - clean; descended the vertical C column to the corridor and swept its west cells - clean; (c) mapped all 6 shelf phases from safety with 6 B-clicks, then rode the 54-row shelf east phase-by-phase (board at P0, walk east 2 cols per phase P1-P4) into the LM room via the cols 18-19 floor hole; (d) baseline D/8 6-click on the LM checker (ring home): no teleport, rotation+phase side-effects only; (e) teleported to the launcher (LM=9/A), clicked a quad button while standing ON the launcher checker: only LM changed - quad is LM-only; (f) drove the ring up 4 (legal), up 8 (refused - rows<=25 void-only), leaving it displaced; teleported back to LM, set D/8, 6-click: no teleport - teleport-to-ring refuted; (g) drove the ring down+left4 to exact concentricity and latched via the 8-bar (assembly merged); no D cell appeared; D/8 6-click post-latch: null; (h) tested fixed-checker hidden twins: launcher 6-click with LM=6/7 null; teleported to R1, set LM=9/A, R1 6-click null - refuting the R1->goal-B-block pairing hypothesis; (i) swept the full LM interior - clean; (j) tested 8-bar/big-B/ACTION5 with LM=D/8 - all normal/no-op; ACTION5 revealed to be an illegal action anyway; (k) discovered wall-bump refusals do NOT tick the row-63 bar but stranding B-presses DO; ground the bar to 64 from a stranded shelf position: at full bar the next press forced the phase through, destroyed the unsupported avatar, and produced GAME_OVER; (l) RESET resumed at L6 start with progress retained and timer zeroed, revealing that level restart restores sockets/quad/8-bar/ring/LM-type; (m) rode west via the 3-tier staircase choreography (54->56->58 tiers descending west, then 58->56->54 rising into the corridor), climbed to R2, re-consumed the socket to re-reveal the quad, rode back east, and tested big-6 on the moving C platform at P5 with all four LM types: all null; (n) final probes: D-pad with LM=D/8 moves the ring normally (no mode change); ring east drive refused at cols 30-37 showing the confinement is tighter than the round-7 law. Ended at 714 env steps, level 6 unsolved, with the D/8-twin creation mechanism as the sole remaining unknown.",
 "gotchas": [
  "dc22 L6 FAIL-TIMER: the row-63 bar ticks ~1 per ~10 actions passively and +1 per refused stranding B-press; at 64 the next stranding B-press is FORCED THROUGH, the avatar dies unsupported, GameState.GAME_OVER. Budget ~600 actions per L6 attempt.",
  "GAME_OVER recovery: action 0 (RESET) resumes at the START of the current level - levels_completed=5 retained, timer zeroed. Death is cheap; do not fear experimenting.",
  "Level restart RESTORES all consumed sockets and re-hides the quad + 8-bar, unlatches the assembly, homes the ring, resets LM to 6/7 - re-tooling costs ~60+ steps (socket re-consume requires the full corridor/R2 round trip).",
  "Quad buttons advance ONLY the lower-middle checker, +1 per click in cycle 6/7->D/8->C/B->9/A (out-of-order click proven). The other three checkers are permanently fixed-type. Quad clicks work remotely from anywhere on the board.",
  "Teleport network is a STAR centered on LM: a fixed checker's 6-click fires only when LM matches its type. No hidden twins exist behind LR/R1/launcher (tested with mismatched LM). D/8 pairs with NOTHING that exists on the board in any tested state (home/displaced/latched ring).",
  "The bare 8-ring obeys the assembly movement law AND a tighter confinement: east drive at rows 26-33 to cols 30-37 was REFUSED despite all-wall/void coverage at rows>=26. The ring/assembly cannot leave the central shaft neighborhood; it can never reach the goal-room band. Do not spend budget on ring/assembly bridging.",
  "The C-colored 2x6 platform (cols 16-21) MOVES with shelf phases: rows 56-57 normally, rows 54-55 at P5 - it is what supports the avatar at (18,54) during P5. It is NOT a teleport object (all 4 LM types tested standing on it).",
  "available_actions is [1,2,3,4,6] on every L6 frame - ACTION5 is illegal input, stop probing it.",
  "Moves: ACTION1=up ACTION2=down ACTION3=left ACTION4=right, 2 cells per step, even-aligned. The small-ring center (cols 9-10) is odd-aligned and can never be stood on.",
  "Shelf choreography EAST (corridor->LM): board 54-shelf at P0 from corridor bottom (step down at cols 6-11), then B->walk-east-2 per phase P1->P4, enter LM hole at cols 18-19 with mv-up from (18,54). WEST (LM->corridor): descend tiers 54->56(P5)->58, B to P0, walk west on 58, rise 58->56, B to P1, west, B to P2, rise at cols 10-11 into the corridor.",
  "Wall-bump refused moves do NOT tick the fail-timer; only stranding B-presses (and passive accrual) do.",
  "The goal sprite IS the solid B block at rows 6-7 cols 46-47 (adapter goal attr = (46,6)) - the win is touching it. All discovered mechanisms are sealed off from the goal room; the ONLY remaining lead is whatever creates the D/8 twin. Everything on the visible control surface has now been exhausted - next round should consider: multi-click quad sequences/timing, interactions while the tick bar is at specific values, or re-examining L1-L5 mechanics for a forward-carrying mechanism.",
  "Full-cycle identity: 4 quad clicks return LM to its type; 2 big-6 clicks return rotation+checker phases to parity. Plan teleport itineraries in pairs."
 ],
